            "evidence": [
              "The full patch for all 50 manifest paths was present in the prompt and I reviewed it. I found no reliability defect that this candidate introduced.",
              "add.go and approve.go both read the skill through one ReadSkillTree call, so linting, the digest and the record come from the same snapshot. A SKILL.md that is a directory or a symlink is refused with a clear message and nothing is written. approve_test.go and add_test.go cover this.",
              "Failure paths are covered by assertions on observable output. They cover symlinks, dangling links, line breaks in file names, a missing SKILL.md, an unreadable tree, version 1 records, other record versions, and a file added, removed, renamed or changed after approval. The digest-by-hand check and the idempotent re-approve check pin determinism. The tests are in skills_approval_digest_cli_test.go, approve_test.go, validate_test.go and add_test.go.",
              "Removing the grandfathering changes the validate summary line and its goldens, and the changelog and README state this. The changes are requested and consistent across the goldens and tests. phase8_acceptance_test.go adds a test that no skill is excused from approval."
            ]
